## Access and participation

Sign-in is required because large-scale automated crawling was placing an
unsustainable load on the service. This is an operational safeguard, not a
change in the intention to keep CommunityCoins source and documentation open.
Public read-only mirrors for material that should remain
available without a Forgejo account are available at [github](https://github.com/communitycoins) and [gitlab](https://gitlab.com/c4319).

Registration remains open, but new accounts are reviewed manually. After
approval, an account can be used to:

- browse the organisations and repositories;
- open issues and join discussions;
- comment and propose changes.

Write or administrative access is granted separately for each repository or
organisation. An approved account therefore provides participation access, not
automatic ownership or publication rights.

## What not to expect

This platform is not organised as:

- a single monolithic project;
- a task tracker first;
- a finished-product showcase.

It is a living codebase whose repositories evolve independently over time.

If you are unsure where to start, read a repository's README, check its Issues
tab, or return to the [CommunityCoins navigation page](https://git.communitycoins.org/).